<Base title="SEO Audit Reading | Full Site Analysis" description="Comprehensive SEO audit for Reading businesses. Technical health, content gaps, backlink analysis, local SEO review. Actionable recommendations." schema={schema}>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="prose">

      <h1>SEO Audit for Reading Businesses</h1>

      <p>SEO Reading offers comprehensive SEO audits that give Reading businesses a clear picture of their search visibility, technical health, and competitive position. An audit is the starting point for any effective SEO campaign because it identifies exactly what is working, what is broken, and where the highest-impact opportunities are.</p>

      <div class="quick-answer">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> An SEO audit is a systematic review of your website's technical health, content, backlinks, and local search presence. For Reading businesses, it reveals why you rank where you do and what specific changes will improve your Google visibility. You receive a prioritised action plan and a 1-hour walkthrough call.
      </div>

      <p>Most Reading businesses we audit have 20-50 actionable issues that are directly suppressing their rankings. Some are quick fixes that produce results within weeks. Others are strategic gaps that require planned content or link building. The audit separates the two and gives you a clear sequence to follow.</p>

      <h2>What's Included in an SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>Our audit covers five pillars that together determine your search visibility in <strong>Reading</strong> and <strong>Berkshire</strong>.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Technical health</strong> — crawlability, indexation, site speed, Core Web Vitals, structured data, HTTPS, mobile usability</li>
        <li><strong>On-page SEO</strong> — title tags, meta descriptions, heading structure, content quality, keyword targeting, internal linking</li>
        <li><strong>Off-page SEO</strong> — backlink profile, referring domain quality, anchor text distribution, toxic link identification</li>
        <li><strong>Local SEO</strong> — Google Business Profile, local citations, NAP consistency, local pack eligibility, review profile</li>
        <li><strong>Competitor analysis</strong> — benchmarking against 3-5 direct competitors in your Reading market</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Each pillar receives a health score, a list of issues ranked by severity, and specific recommendations with expected impact.</p>

      <h2>Technical Health Assessment</h2>

      <p>The technical assessment is the largest section of the audit. We crawl your entire site using Screaming Frog and cross-reference findings with Google Search Console data.</p>

      <h3>What We Check</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Crawlability</strong> — are all important pages reachable? Are robots.txt and meta robots correctly configured? Are there crawl errors in Search Console?</li>
        <li><strong>Indexation</strong> — which pages are indexed, which are excluded, and why? Are canonical tags correctly pointing? Is there index bloat from duplicate or thin pages?</li>
        <li><strong>Site speed</strong> — Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) from field data and lab testing. Page-by-page speed analysis for your highest-traffic URLs.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured data</strong> — is schema markup present? Is it valid? Are you missing schema types that could earn rich results? For Reading businesses, LocalBusiness schema is critical.</li>
        <li><strong>HTTPS</strong> — SSL certificate validity, mixed content, redirect implementation from HTTP to HTTPS.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile usability</strong> — responsive design issues, touch target sizes, viewport configuration, mobile-specific speed.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>For a deeper look at what technical SEO involves and why it matters, see our <a href="/technical-seo-reading/">technical SEO services page</a>.</p>

      <h2>Content and Keyword Gap Analysis</h2>

      <p>Your content determines what queries you can rank for. The content audit identifies missed opportunities in the Reading market that your competitors are capturing and you are not.</p>

      <h3>What We Analyse</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Current keyword rankings</strong> — every query your site appears for in Google, with position, impressions, clicks, and CTR</li>
        <li><strong>Keyword gaps</strong> — queries your competitors rank for that you do not, filtered to Reading-relevant terms</li>
        <li><strong>Content quality</strong> — thin pages, duplicate content, outdated information, pages that target the same keyword (cannibalisation)</li>
        <li><strong>Search intent alignment</strong> — are your pages matching what Google wants to show for each query?</li>
        <li><strong>Striking distance keywords</strong> — queries where you rank positions 4-20 and a content improvement could push you into the top 3</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The output is a prioritised list of content opportunities with estimated search volume and recommended page formats. Many Reading businesses discover that a handful of content improvements can double their organic traffic within 3-6 months.</p>

      <h2>Backlink Profile Review</h2>

      <p>Backlinks remain one of Google's strongest ranking signals. The backlink review examines the quality and quantity of sites linking to yours.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Referring domain count and quality</strong> — how many unique sites link to you, and what is their authority?</li>
        <li><strong>Anchor text distribution</strong> — is the anchor text natural or does it suggest manipulative link building?</li>
        <li><strong>Toxic links</strong> — are there spammy or harmful links that could trigger a Google penalty?</li>
        <li><strong>Link velocity</strong> — are you gaining or losing links over time?</li>
        <li><strong>Competitor comparison</strong> — how does your backlink profile compare to Reading competitors in your industry?</li>
      </ul>

      <p>For most Reading businesses, the backlink review reveals that competitors have more links from local directories, industry bodies, and Berkshire-based publications. We identify the specific link sources you should target.</p>

      <h2>Local SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>Local SEO determines whether your business appears in Google's local pack — the map results shown for location-based queries. For Reading businesses, this is often the highest-converting search real estate.</p>

      <h3>Google Business Profile</h3>

      <p>We review your Google Business Profile for completeness, accuracy, and optimisation. This includes your business categories, description, photos, opening hours, service area, Q&A, and posts. A fully optimised GBP is the single most important local ranking factor.</p>

      <h3>Citations and NAP Consistency</h3>

      <p>Your business name, address, and phone number (NAP) must be consistent across every directory, social profile, and mention online. Inconsistencies confuse Google and weaken local rankings. We check the major UK directories — Yell, Thomson Local, Yelp, Cylex, FreeIndex — and Reading-specific directories for accuracy.</p>

      <h3>Local Pack Eligibility</h3>

      <p>Not every query triggers a local pack. We identify which of your target keywords show local pack results and whether your business is eligible to appear. For <strong>Reading</strong> businesses competing with firms in <strong>Wokingham</strong>, <strong>Bracknell</strong>, and <strong>Newbury</strong>, local pack visibility can be the deciding factor in winning a customer.</p>

      <h2>Competitor Analysis</h2>

      <p>An audit without competitive context is incomplete. We benchmark your site against 3-5 direct competitors — businesses that rank for the same Reading-area keywords you want to win.</p>

      <p>The competitor analysis covers:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Domain authority and backlink profile comparison</li>
        <li>Content depth and keyword coverage gaps</li>
        <li>Technical health comparison (speed, mobile, structured data)</li>
        <li>Local SEO presence (GBP reviews, local citations, local content)</li>
        <li>SERP feature ownership (featured snippets, People Also Ask, local pack positions)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>This tells you exactly where you need to invest to overtake specific competitors. For a Reading accountancy firm, that might mean creating service pages for specific tax topics their competitors rank for. For a Reading restaurant, it might mean building a review profile that matches the local pack leaders.</p>

      <h2>What You Receive</h2>

      <p>The audit deliverable is practical and actionable. You receive three things:</p>

      <h3>1. Comprehensive Audit Report</h3>

      <p>A detailed document covering every finding across all five pillars. Each issue is described with screenshots, severity rating, and a specific recommendation. The report typically runs 30-60 pages depending on site size.</p>

      <h3>2. Prioritised Action Plan</h3>

      <p>A spreadsheet ranking every recommendation by impact and effort. High-impact, low-effort items are at the top. This is your roadmap — work through it from top to bottom for maximum results in minimum time. Issues are tagged as critical, high, medium, or low priority.</p>

      <h3>3. One-Hour Walkthrough Call</h3>

      <p>We walk through the findings with you, answer questions, and discuss implementation options. This ensures you understand not just what to fix, but why each issue matters and what results to expect. Many Reading business owners find this is the most valuable part of the audit because it translates technical findings into business terms.</p>

      <h2>Who Needs an SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>An SEO audit is relevant at several stages of a Reading business's online journey.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>New businesses</strong> near <strong>The Oracle</strong> or <strong>Broad Street</strong> launching their first website need a baseline to build from</li>
        <li><strong>Established firms</strong> at <strong>Forbury Square</strong> or <strong>Kings Road</strong> whose rankings have plateaued or declined</li>
        <li><strong>Post-redesign</strong> — any business that has recently changed their website design, CMS, or URL structure</li>
        <li><strong>Post-penalty</strong> — businesses that have experienced a sudden, significant ranking drop</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-investment</strong> — before committing to an SEO retainer, an audit tells you exactly what you are investing in</li>
        <li><strong>Competitive pressure</strong> — when a competitor suddenly starts outranking you for your core Reading-area keywords</li>
      </ul>

      <p>If you have never had an SEO audit, there are almost certainly quick wins sitting on your site right now. The audit finds them.</p>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">How long does an SEO audit take?</h3>
        <p>A comprehensive SEO audit for a typical Reading business website takes 7-14 working days. This includes the crawl, data analysis, report writing, and preparation of your prioritised action plan. Larger sites with thousands of pages may take longer. You will receive a confirmed delivery date when you book.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">What do I need to provide for the audit?</h3>
        <p>We need Google Search Console access (or to be added as a user), Google Analytics access if available, and your top business goals. If you have specific keywords you are targeting or competitors you want to benchmark against, share those too. We handle everything else.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">How much does an SEO audit cost?</h3>
        <p>Our comprehensive SEO audit is a fixed-fee service. The exact cost depends on site size and complexity. Visit our <a href="/seo-pricing-reading/">pricing page</a> for indicative rates, or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> for a quote tailored to your site.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">Will you implement the recommendations or just report them?</h3>
        <p>The audit deliverable is a report with prioritised recommendations. Implementation is available as a separate engagement or as part of an ongoing SEO retainer. Many Reading businesses choose to start with the audit and then move into monthly SEO management for implementation and monitoring.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">How often should I get an SEO audit?</h3>
        <p>A full audit every 12 months is a good baseline. If you have recently redesigned your site, migrated platforms, or experienced a significant ranking drop, an immediate audit is warranted. Between full audits, ongoing monitoring catches issues as they appear.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">Do you audit competitor websites as part of the process?</h3>
        <p>Yes. We benchmark your site against 3-5 direct competitors in the Reading market. This reveals gaps in content, backlinks, and technical implementation that you can exploit. We identify specifically what your competitors do better and where you already have an advantage.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-box">
        <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Book Your SEO Audit</h2>
        <p>Get a clear picture of your website's search performance and a prioritised action plan to improve it. Every audit includes a 1-hour walkthrough call.</p>
        <a href="/contact/">Get in Touch</a>
      </div>

      <p>Want a quick health check first? Our <a href="/free-seo-audit-reading/">free SEO audit</a> gives you a baseline assessment with no obligation. See our <a href="/seo-pricing-reading/">pricing page</a> for service costs, or learn about <a href="/technical-seo-reading/">technical SEO</a> specifically.</p>

      <p>Back to <a href="/services/">all services</a> or return to <a href="/">SEO Reading homepage</a>.</p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
